[I] Wake On LAN functionality in a small program

[T] wol is a Wake On LAN client that wakes up magic packet compliant
[T] machines, such as computers with wake-on-lan capable ethernet cards. It
[T] also supports the password protected SecureON extension provided by some
[T] workstations.

[U] https://wake-on-lan.sourceforge.io/

[A] Wol Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

[V] 0.7.1
[L] GPL

[D] 15d367100e061ca92026bf07a0b2eef875b96f365bd0b1020101446a wol-0.7.1.tar.gz https://prdownloads.sourceforge.net/sourceforge/wake-on-lan/

atstage cross && export jm_cv_func_working_malloc=yes jm_cv_func_working_realloc=yes
var_append CC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' -std=gnu17
